# Nginx-set-conf Project Rules

# git commit rules
- use short commit messages
- use the present tense
- use the imperative mood
- Start with [ADD], [FIX], [CHG], [UPDATE], [REMOVE]

# File naming conventions
*.py should be snake_case
*.yaml should be snake_case
*.md should be UPPERCASE

# Python code style
*.py should follow PEP 8
*.py should have docstrings for all public functions and classes
*.py should use type hints for function parameters
*.py should use absolute imports
*.py should have module-level docstrings

# Template conventions
nginx_set_conf/config_templates.py should include date comments in format "# DD.MM.YYYY"
nginx_set_conf/config_templates.py should use consistent indentation in nginx configs
nginx_set_conf/config_templates.py should include "#authentication" marker before auth settings

# Documentation requirements
README.md should include all supported templates
README.md should include usage examples
README.md should include installation instructions

# Version control
__init__.py should contain version number
setup.py should match version in __init__.py

# Configuration files
yaml_examples/**/*.yaml should include commented auth_file option
yaml_examples/**/*.yaml should use consistent indentation
yaml_examples/**/*.yaml should include empty values for customization

# Security practices
*.py should not contain hardcoded credentials
*.yaml should not contain real credentials
nginx configs should include security headers
nginx configs should include SSL/TLS settings

# Logging
*.py should use the logging module
*.py should include rotating file handlers
*.py should include console handlers

# Error handling
*.py should include appropriate error handling
*.py should provide meaningful error messages

# Testing
tests/ should include unit tests for all templates
tests/ should include integration tests

# Dependencies
setup.py should specify minimum Python version >= 3.8
setup.py should list all required dependencies

# License
All files should include AGPL-3.0 license header 